# Procedural Flipbook Flipping Animation (Stack Landing & Zero-Cutting Dynamic Cascade)
#
# Key Geometric Principles:
# 1. Natural Top-to-Bottom Stacking on Both Sides:
#    - Right Stack: Page j (0 = top, n-1 = bottom) sits at height (n - 1 - j) * t.
#    - Left Stack: Page j lands ON TOP of previously turned pages at height j * t.
#    - Currently turning page always descends through the air and lands on top of the left stack.
# 2. Continuous Spine Transition:
#    - The binding edge transitions smoothly across the spine width S = (n - 1) * t.
#    - Pages stay permanently anchored to the book binding.
# 3. Monotonic Delayed Paper Curl:
#    - Root angle: s_root(p) = 3p^2 - 2p^3
#    - Tip angle: s_tip(p) = smoothstep(p^(1 + bend_strength))
#    - Strictly monotonic angle field: zero page intersection / zero mid-air cutting!
# 4. Solid Manifold Geometry with Clean Normals.
# 5. Flush Non-Intersecting Hard Bound & Paper Bound Cover with Dynamic Connected Spine (Z <= 0.0).
